{
  "description": "Private subscriptions and server-side sign-outs (asyncapi.yaml, 'Private subscriptions ... end, without any frame, in three cases'). Each case is a script run against the SDK's WebSocket client over a scripted server. Step kinds: {\"client\": \"auth\", \"token\": T} calls the public auth method; {\"client\": \"subscribe\", \"channels\": [...]} calls the public subscribe method (a client call that is refused by the server, such as a failed auth, may raise or reject: the runner ignores that error and goes on); {\"server\": FRAME, \"reply_to\": \"auth\"|\"subscribe\"} sends FRAME with the id of the SDK's most recent unanswered request of that op (no reply_to: the frame is sent as given, an unsolicited event); {\"expect_sent\": [...]} compares the frames the SDK sent since the previous expect_sent (ignoring ping), in order, on op and channels/token only (ids are not compared); {\"expect_events\": [...]} compares the tracked events emitted since the previous expect_events, as a set (order within one step is free), on the fields given; {\"expect_held\": [...]} compares the channels the client holds, as a set; {\"expect_token\": true|false} says whether the client still keeps a token for re-authentication. Tracked events (names map to each SDK's idiom): auth_changed {reason: user_changed | auth_failed | session_revoked, previous_user_id, user_id, code (auth_failed only), dropped (set of private channels the client stopped holding)}; resync {reason: \"reauth\"} (private channels were re-subscribed after a sign-out: refetch private state); auth_lost (the existing session-revoked event). Rules: (1) an authenticated ack whose user_id differs from the previous successful auth on this connection drops the held private channels and re-subscribes them at once; the same user_id changes nothing. (2) An error frame whose id is an auth request's id (any code) signs out: held private channels are dropped and kept as pending, the token is forgotten. (3) session.revoked with data.current === true signs out the same way and still emits auth_lost; current false or missing changes nothing. (4) After the next successful auth, pending private channels are re-subscribed and resync {reason: reauth} is emitted, only when there were pending channels. (5) An UNAUTHENTICATED error with a subscribe request's id is a refused subscribe, not a sign-out. Private channels: orders, balances, deposits, withdrawals, account. An expected event list that is empty means no tracked event.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "reauth_other_account",
      "steps": [
        {
          "client": "auth",
          "token": "tok_a"
        },
        {
          "server": {
            "type": "authenticated",
            "user_id": "aaaa0001"
          },
          "reply_to": "auth"
        },
        {
          "client": "subscribe",
          "channels": [
            "orders",
            "ticker:BTC/USDT"
          ]
        },
        {
          "server": {
            "type": "subscribed",
            "channels": [
              "orders",
              "ticker:BTC/USDT"
            ]
          },
          "reply_to": "subscribe"
        },
        {
          "expect_sent": [
            {
              "op": "auth",
              "token": "tok_a"
            },
            {
              "op": "subscribe",
              "channels": [
                "orders",
                "ticker:BTC/USDT"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "expect_events": []
        },
        {
          "client": "auth",
          "token": "tok_b"
        },
        {
          "server": {
            "type": "authenticated",
            "user_id": "bbbb0002"
          },
          "reply_to": "auth"
        },
        {
          "expect_sent": [
            {
              "op": "auth",
              "token": "tok_b"
            },
            {
              "op": "subscribe",
              "channels": [
                "orders"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "server": {
            "type": "subscribed",
            "channels": [
              "orders"
            ]
          },
          "reply_to": "subscribe"
        },
        {
          "expect_events": [
            {
              "type": "auth_changed",
              "reason": "user_changed",
              "previous_user_id": "aaaa0001",
              "user_id": "bbbb0002",
              "dropped": [
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "resync",
              "reason": "reauth"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "expect_held": [
            "orders",
            "ticker:BTC/USDT"
          ]
        },
        {
          "expect_token": true
        }
      ]
    },
